{"header":"<h1>Module <code><span>Eio.Domain_manager</span></code></h1>","type":"documentation","uses_katex":false,"breadcrumbs":[{"name":"Index","href":"../../../index.html","kind":"leaf-page"},{"name":"eio","href":"../../index.html","kind":"page"},{"name":"Eio","href":"../index.html","kind":"module"},{"name":"Domain_manager","href":"#","kind":"module"}],"toc":[{"title":"Provider Interface","href":"#provider-interface","children":[]}],"source_anchor":null,"preamble":"<p>Parallel computation across multiple CPU cores.</p>","content":"<div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-ty\"><a href=\"#type-ty\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> ty</span><span> = </span><span>[ </span></code><ol><li id=\"type-ty.Domain_mgr\" class=\"def variant constructor anchored\"><a href=\"#type-ty.Domain_mgr\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span>| </span><span>`Domain_mgr</span></code></li></ol><code><span> ]</span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec type anchored\" id=\"type-t\"><a href=\"#type-t\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">type</span> <span>'a t</span></span><span> = <span><span>(<span>[&gt; <a href=\"#type-ty\">ty</a> ]</span> <span class=\"keyword\">as</span> 'a)</span> <a href=\"../Resource/index.html#type-t\">Resource.t</a></span></span></code></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-run\"><a href=\"#val-run\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> run : <span><span><span class=\"type-var\">_</span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span>(<span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>run t f</code> runs <code>f ()</code> in a newly-created domain and returns the result.</p><p>Other fibers in the calling domain can run in parallel with the new domain.</p><p>Warning: <code>f</code> must only access thread-safe values from the calling domain, but this is not enforced by the type system.</p><p>If the calling fiber is cancelled, this is propagated to the spawned domain.</p></div></div><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec value anchored\" id=\"val-run_raw\"><a href=\"#val-run_raw\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">val</span> run_raw : <span><span><span class=\"type-var\">_</span> <a href=\"#type-t\">t</a></span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span><span>(<span>unit <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span>)</span> <span class=\"arrow\">&#45;&gt;</span></span> <span class=\"type-var\">'a</span></span></code></div><div class=\"spec-doc\"><p><code>run_raw t f</code> is like <a href=\"#val-run\"><code>run</code></a>, but does not run an event loop in the new domain, and so cannot perform IO, fork fibers, etc.</p></div></div><h3 id=\"provider-interface\"><a href=\"#provider-interface\" class=\"anchor\"></a>Provider Interface</h3><div class=\"odoc-spec\"><div class=\"spec module anchored\" id=\"module-Pi\"><a href=\"#module-Pi\" class=\"anchor\"></a><code><span><span class=\"keyword\">module</span> <a href=\"Pi/index.html\">Pi</a></span><span> : <span class=\"keyword\">sig</span> ... <span class=\"keyword\">end</span></span></code></div></div>"}